WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:19.307
<v Host>Welcome to Japanese Daily News. I'm Maya. Today is July tenth. A large, very powerful typhoon is bearing down on Okinawa's southern islands right now. Today's story is about the warnings and what people there are being told to do. Let's listen.

00:00:19.908 --> 00:00:22.859
<v News>今日のニュースです。

00:00:23.559 --> 00:00:26.800
<v News>台風のニュースです。

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:35.131
<v News>大型で非常に強い台風9号が、沖縄に近づいています。

00:00:35.832 --> 00:00:46.200
<v News>台風は、11日の午前中に、沖縄の先島諸島にかなり接近する見込みです。

00:00:46.899 --> 00:00:56.020
<v News>気象庁は、宮古島などの地域に、厳重に警戒するよう呼びかけています。

00:00:56.719 --> 00:01:08.408
<v News>11日に予想される最大風速は45メートル、最大瞬間風速は60メートルです。

00:01:09.108 --> 00:01:16.236
<v News>これは、人が外で立っていられないほどの、猛烈な風です。

00:01:16.936 --> 00:01:23.680
<v News>先島諸島では、一部の家が壊れるおそれもあります。

00:01:24.379 --> 00:01:32.299
<v News>海も大きく荒れて、高い波や高潮にも注意が必要です。

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:40.584
<v News>強い雨が続き、土砂災害や川の氾濫の危険もあります。

00:01:41.284 --> 00:01:48.772
<v News>飛行機や船が欠航するなど、交通への影響も出ています。

00:01:49.471 --> 00:01:56.959
<v News>気象庁は、早めに安全な場所へ避難するよう伝えています。

00:01:57.659 --> 00:02:05.819
<v News>危険なので、外に出ないで、丈夫な建物の中で過ごしてください。

00:02:06.519 --> 00:02:14.872
<v News>台風はそのあと、東シナ海を進んで、台湾に向かう見込みです。

00:02:15.572 --> 00:02:19.364
<v Host>Now let's break it down, sentence by sentence.

00:02:19.963 --> 00:02:28.147
<v Slow>大型で非常に強い台風9号が、沖縄に近づいています。

00:02:28.948 --> 00:02:33.460
<v Host>A large, very strong Typhoon No. 9 is approaching Okinawa.

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:36.340
<v Vocab>大型

00:02:36.740 --> 00:02:38.876
<v Host>It means large in scale.

00:02:39.475 --> 00:02:41.924
<v Vocab>近づく

00:02:42.324 --> 00:02:45.419
<v Host>It means to approach or come closer.

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:57.132
<v Slow>台風は、11日の午前中に、沖縄の先島諸島にかなり接近する見込みです。

00:02:57.931 --> 00:03:04.771
<v Host>The typhoon is expected to come quite close to Okinawa's Sakishima Islands on the morning of the eleventh.

00:03:05.372 --> 00:03:07.723
<v Vocab>接近

00:03:08.123 --> 00:03:10.163
<v Host>It means a close approach.

00:03:10.764 --> 00:03:12.972
<v Vocab>見込み

00:03:13.372 --> 00:03:17.451
<v Host>It means an expectation or forecast of what will happen.

00:03:18.051 --> 00:03:27.819
<v Slow>気象庁は、宮古島などの地域に、厳重に警戒するよう呼びかけています。

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:34.692
<v Host>The Meteorological Agency is urging areas such as Miyakojima to be on strict guard.

00:03:35.292 --> 00:03:37.644
<v Vocab>警戒

00:03:38.044 --> 00:03:41.692
<v Host>It means caution or being on guard against danger.

00:03:42.292 --> 00:03:44.883
<v Vocab>呼びかける

00:03:45.283 --> 00:03:48.883
<v Host>It means to call on or urge people to do something.

00:03:49.484 --> 00:04:02.012
<v Slow>11日に予想される最大風速は45メートル、最大瞬間風速は60メートルです。

00:04:02.812 --> 00:04:10.228
<v Host>The maximum wind speed expected on the eleventh is forty-five meters per second, with gusts up to sixty.

00:04:10.828 --> 00:04:13.924
<v Vocab>最大風速

00:04:14.324 --> 00:04:17.468
<v Host>It means the maximum sustained wind speed.

00:04:18.067 --> 00:04:25.699
<v Slow>これは、人が外で立っていられないほどの、猛烈な風です。

00:04:26.500 --> 00:04:31.923
<v Host>This is a violent wind, so strong that a person cannot stay standing outside.

00:04:32.524 --> 00:04:34.923
<v Vocab>猛烈

00:04:35.324 --> 00:04:37.819
<v Host>It means fierce or violent.

00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:45.644
<v Slow>先島諸島では、一部の家が壊れるおそれもあります。

00:04:46.444 --> 00:04:52.348
<v Host>In the Sakishima Islands, there is even a risk that some houses could be destroyed.

00:04:52.947 --> 00:04:55.252
<v Vocab>壊れる

00:04:55.651 --> 00:04:58.315
<v Host>It means to break or be destroyed.

00:04:58.915 --> 00:05:01.004
<v Vocab>おそれ

00:05:01.403 --> 00:05:05.315
<v Host>It means a risk or fear that something bad may happen.

00:05:05.915 --> 00:05:14.387
<v Slow>海も大きく荒れて、高い波や高潮にも注意が必要です。

00:05:15.187 --> 00:05:20.708
<v Host>The sea is also very rough, and caution is needed for high waves and storm surge.

00:05:21.307 --> 00:05:23.732
<v Vocab>高潮

00:05:24.132 --> 00:05:28.572
<v Host>It means a storm surge, when the sea level rises abnormally.

00:05:29.172 --> 00:05:31.163
<v Vocab>波

00:05:31.564 --> 00:05:33.124
<v Host>It means a wave.

00:05:33.723 --> 00:05:41.836
<v Slow>強い雨が続き、土砂災害や川の氾濫の危険もあります。

00:05:42.636 --> 00:05:48.516
<v Host>Heavy rain continues, and there is also a danger of landslides and rivers overflowing.

00:05:49.115 --> 00:05:51.827
<v Vocab>土砂災害

00:05:52.228 --> 00:05:55.468
<v Host>It means a landslide or sediment disaster.

00:05:56.067 --> 00:05:58.300
<v Vocab>氾濫

00:05:58.699 --> 00:06:01.555
<v Host>It means flooding, when a river overflows.

00:06:02.156 --> 00:06:10.172
<v Slow>気象庁は、早めに安全な場所へ避難するよう伝えています。

00:06:10.971 --> 00:06:15.675
<v Host>The agency is telling people to evacuate to a safe place early.

00:06:16.276 --> 00:06:18.363
<v Vocab>避難

00:06:18.764 --> 00:06:22.339
<v Host>It means evacuation, moving to a safe place.

00:06:22.939 --> 00:06:31.675
<v Slow>危険なので、外に出ないで、丈夫な建物の中で過ごしてください。

00:06:32.475 --> 00:06:38.115
<v Host>Because it's dangerous, please stay inside a sturdy building and don't go outside.

00:06:38.716 --> 00:06:40.923
<v Vocab>丈夫

00:06:41.324 --> 00:06:44.252
<v Host>Here it means sturdy or solidly built.

00:06:44.851 --> 00:06:46.915
<v Vocab>危険

00:06:47.315 --> 00:06:49.980
<v Host>It means danger or dangerous.

00:06:50.579 --> 00:06:53.579
<v Host>Let's listen to the whole story one more time.

